From 37c452ad3d9a81251b3c7e2a1d853e38c0208096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A3 <a3@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:07:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1711/1712] application: use the SDK width types the app
 helpers declare

NitroSDK s32/u32 are long on 3DS, so GCC 14 rejects passing the game int
locals and BOOL flags to helpers that take s32*/u32* (TextOBJ_GetPosition,
System_GetTouchHeldCoords, DressUpGfx_GetSlot*, DressUp_Start*Transition,
CodeEntryArgs_New, ManagedSprite_GetPositionFxXYWithSubscreenOffset,
SwalotPlop_CalcArcStep, MimeJrTopOffsets). Under SDK_PORT_3DS give the
locals the callee exact type, or cast the same-width pointer at the call
site where the object belongs to another header (DressUpWork.transitionDone);
the DS text stays under #else. Also restore the int return type of the
PokedexApp_MainSeq_62 definition, which already has a static int prototype.

Fixes the 3DS compile of src/application/{ball_capsule_editor,
plaza_game_mime_jr_top,plaza_game_swalot_plop,wobbuffet_pop_scene}.c and
src/application/{dress_up/dress_up,palpad/palpad_friend_code,
pc_box/pc_box_ui,pokedex/pokedex_main_seq}.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
